{
  "title": "Add Batch Result Validation and Automatic Retry for Failed Records",
  "issue": "N/A",
  "priority": "high",
  "type": "feature",
  "status": "📋 PLANNED",
  "description": "Implement validation to detect missing records by comparing sent vs received custom_ids, then automatically resubmit failed records as new batches. Uses Dead Letter Queue (DLQ) pattern to ensure no data loss. Creates audit artifacts (retry manifest and DLQ file) for compliance, debugging, and monitoring.",

  "executive_summary": {
    "problem": "Batch APIs process all records together but some fail (rate limits, malformed data, internal errors). Provider marks batch as 'completed' with counts like '237 completed, 4 failed of 241 total'. The 4 failed records are lost - users must manually identify and resubmit them.",
    "solution": "After batch completes: (1) Compare sent custom_ids vs received custom_ids to detect failures, (2) Automatically resubmit missing records as NEW batch (DLQ pattern), (3) Track parent-child relationship, (4) Merge results when retry batch completes, (5) Create audit artifacts for compliance and debugging.",
    "impact": "Zero data loss - failed records automatically retried. Users don't need to manually identify failures. Industry-standard DLQ pattern. Clear error messages with specific missing IDs and retry_batch_id for manual intervention if needed. Complete audit trail via retry manifest (compliance ready). DLQ file for permanently failed records (manual recovery).",
    "implementation": "Add validation methods, implement record-level retry with batch resubmission, track parent-child batches in registry, create audit artifacts (retry manifest + DLQ file), provide merge utility for results",
    "testing": "Unit tests for validation logic, integration tests for retry and merge, artifact creation tests, manual testing with intentional failures",
    "code_changes": "~1,795 lines added across batch_service.py and test files (includes 215 lines for audit artifacts)"
  },

