    "phase_9_user_configuration": {
      "status": "✅ COMPLETED",
      "completed_date": "2025-10-09",
      "priority": "medium",
      "description": "Allow users to configure max retry depth via agent config",
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "add_config_loading",
          "title": "Add method to load retry config from agent_config",
          "file": "agent_actions/tasks/services/batch_service.py",
          "purpose": "Load user-configured max retry depth from agent_config",
          "signature": "def _load_retry_config(self, agent_config: Optional[Dict[str, Any]]) -> int",
          "returns": "int - max_retry_depth",
          "logic": [
            "1. Default value: 2",
            "2. If agent_config is None, return default",
            "3. Check agent_config['batch_retry']['max_retry_depth']",
            "4. Validate: must be non-negative integer",
            "5. Return max_retry_depth"
          ],
          "implementation": "def _load_retry_config(self, agent_config: Optional[Dict[str, Any]]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Load retry configuration from agent config.\n    \n    Args:\n        agent_config: Agent configuration dict\n        \n    Returns:\n        max_retry_depth\n    \"\"\"\n    max_retry_depth = self._MAX_RETRY_DEPTH\n    \n    if not agent_config:\n        return max_retry_depth\n    \n    batch_retry_config = agent_config.get('batch_retry', {})\n    \n    if 'max_retry_depth' in batch_retry_config:\n        depth = batch_retry_config['max_retry_depth']\n        if isinstance(depth, int) and depth >= 0:\n            max_retry_depth = depth\n        else:\n            print(f\"[WARN] Invalid max_retry_depth: {depth}. Using default {self._MAX_RETRY_DEPTH}\")\n    \n    return max_retry_depth",
          "lines_added": 30
        },
        {
          "id": "use_config_in_methods",
          "title": "Use loaded config in retry methods",
          "file": "agent_actions/tasks/services/batch_service.py",
          "changes": [
            "In _resubmit_missing_records_as_batch: load config and use instead of class constant",
            "Pass agent_config to method from orchestration layer"
          ],
          "lines_modified": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "document_config_schema",
          "title": "Document agent_config schema for batch_retry",
          "file": "agent_actions/tasks/services/batch_service.py",
          "location": "Module docstring or class docstring",
          "content": "\"\"\"\nAgent Config Schema for Batch Retry:\n\n{\n  \"batch_retry\": {\n    \"max_retry_depth\": 2  // Optional, default 2. Record-level retry depth (3 total attempts per record).\n  }\n}\n\nExample:\n{\n  \"model_name\": \"gpt-4\",\n  \"batch_retry\": {\n    \"max_retry_depth\": 1  // Only one retry attempt per record\n  }\n}\n\"\"\"",
          "lines_added": 15
        }
      ],
      "validation_requirements": [
        "✅ Loads config from agent_config['batch_retry']",
        "✅ Falls back to class default if not provided",
        "✅ Validates config values (non-negative integers)",
        "✅ Logs warnings for invalid values",
        "✅ Documented schema in docstring"
      ],
      "estimated_lines": 50
    },

    "phase_9b_agent_config_documentation": {
      "priority": "medium",
      "description": "Document batch_retry configuration in agent config schema and examples",
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "document_batch_retry_in_examples",
          "title": "Add batch_retry example to agent config documentation",
          "file": "docs/agent-configuration.md (or similar)",
          "content": "## Batch Retry Configuration\n\nYou can configure automatic retry behavior for batch operations:\n\n```yaml\nagent_type: batch\nname: process_customers\nmodel_name: gpt-4\nbatch_retry:\n  max_retry_depth: 2  # Max retry attempts per failed record (default: 2)\n```\n\n### Retry Behavior\n\n- **max_retry_depth**: Maximum number of retry attempts for failed records\n  - Default: 2 (total 3 attempts: initial + 2 retries)\n  - Range: 0-10 (0 disables retry)\n  - Each retry creates a new batch with only the failed records\n  - Records exceeding max depth are written to Dead Letter Queue (DLQ)\n\n### Example Workflow\n\n1. Submit batch with 100 records\n2. 95 succeed, 5 fail → Automatic retry batch created\n3. 4 succeed on retry, 1 fails → Second retry batch created\n4. If max_retry_depth exceeded → Record written to DLQ file\n\n### Audit Files\n\n- `{batch_name}_retry_manifest.json`: Complete audit trail\n- `{batch_name}_dlq.jsonl`: Permanently failed records\n",
          "lines_added": 30
        }
      ],
      "validation_requirements": [
        "✅ batch_retry configuration documented",
        "✅ max_retry_depth parameter explained",
        "✅ Audit files documented",
        "✅ Example workflow shown"
      ],
      "estimated_lines": 30
    },

